# LF in the repository and in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says. Git for Windows sets
# core.autocrlf=true system-wide, which otherwise checks every file out as CRLF, and Prettier (endOfLine
# "lf") then flags all of them (TOOL-9). Files git detects as binary are left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Raw HTTP/1.1 captures from OkHttp: CRLF is part of the wire format and tests split on "\r\n\r\n"
# (packages/fixtures/README.md), so these stay byte-exact.
packages/fixtures/http/*.http -text
